{"title":"Ugly Number III","difficulty":"Medium","statement":"An ugly number is a positive integer that is divisible by a, b, or c.\nGiven four integers n, a, b, and c, return the nth ugly number.\n\n## Examples\n\n```text\nInput: n = 3, a = 2, b = 3, c = 5\nOutput: 4\n```\n\nThe ugly numbers are 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 8, 9, 10... The 3rd is 4.\n\n```text\nInput: n = 4, a = 2, b = 3, c = 4\nOutput: 6\n```\n\nThe ugly numbers are 2, 3, 4, 6, 8, 9, 10, 12... The 4th is 6.\n\n```text\nInput: n = 5, a = 2, b = 11, c = 13\nOutput: 10\n```\n\nThe ugly numbers are 2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 11, 12, 13... The 5th is 10.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- 1 <= n, a, b, c <= 10^9\n- 1 <= a * b * c <= 10^18\n- It is guaranteed that the result will be in range [1, 2 * 10^9].\n","starterCode":"class Solution:\n    def nthUglyNumber(self, n: int, a: int, b: int, c: int) -> int:\n        pass\n","entryPoint":"Solution().nthUglyNumber","parameters":[{"name":"n","type":"int"},{"name":"a","type":"int"},{"name":"b","type":"int"},{"name":"c","type":"int"}],"returnType":"int","tests":[{"input":[1,1,1,1],"expected":1},{"input":[10,754666,880900,418197],"expected":2263998},{"input":[1000000000,1000000000,1,1],"expected":1000000000},{"input":[1000000000,2,2,2],"expected":2000000000},{"input":[1000000000,2,217983653,336916467],"expected":1999999984},{"input":[100021,378559,4712,72744],"expected":437561032},{"input":[1001,502513,220806,762478],"expected":128067480},{"input":[10061,639306,343684,95032],"expected":670925920},{"input":[10085,107564,559130,609065],"expected":792423988},{"input":[1019,979282,354278,682070],"expected":192018676},{"input":[10214,630413,21548,412931],"expected":202615844},{"input":[10249,161766,953215,541692],"expected":1129288446},{"input":[1027,330093,411722,949242],"expected":157784454},{"input":[10306,638058,619738,138980],"expected":993429040},{"input":[10444,167856,251046,233936],"expected":734792976},{"input":[10454,635809,925717,89780],"expected":758102320},{"input":[10459,155611,591297,4